[Kind "for-us"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bc4 Nxe4 5. Nxe4 ( 5. Bxf7+? { Gives up the bishop for one pawn and drags the king to f7, where Black's pieces soon attack it. } 5... Kxf7 6. Nxe4 d5 7. Ng3 e4 { Hits the knight on f3 and gains time. } ) 5... d5 6. Bxd5? { Takes the pawn that did the forking. Material stays level, but White's king is stuck in the middle and Black's pieces arrive first. } 6... Qxd5 { The queen attacks the loose knight on e4 and the pawn on g2 at once. } 7. Nc3 7... Qd6 { Keeps the queen safe and ready to join the attack. } 8. O-O 8... Bg4 { Pins the knight on f3 to the queen on d1. Black follows with ...Bh5 and ...O-O-O. } 9. h3 9... Bh5 *
